# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in YOUR project's values.
# .env is git-ignored — never commit real values.
#
# Only the two values below are allowed in the frontend.
# They are safe to expose ONLY because Supabase Row Level Security (RLS)
# protects every table. See supabase/README.md.
#
# NEVER put these anywhere in this project or repository:
#   - Supabase service_role key
#   - Supabase database password
#   - Any admin password

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- SERVER-SIDE ONLY: Email foundation (Phase C / C4) ---
# The variables below are NOT frontend settings. They are the
# names of secrets that live ONLY in the Supabase Dashboard
# (Edge Functions > Secrets) for supabase/functions/send-email.
# They are listed here so the names are documented in one place.
# NEVER write real values into this file, into .env, or anywhere
# in this repository — and the Gmail App Password must never be
# shared in chat. See supabase/functions/README.md.
#
# GMAIL_ADDRESS=
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=
# INTERNAL_FUNCTION_SECRET=
#
# --- Subscriber system (Phase C / C2), same server-only rule ---
# PUBLIC_SITE_URL=            (public site base, for email links)
# UNSUBSCRIBE_SIGNING_SECRET= (owner-generated random string)

# --- Future: CAPTCHA for the contact form (NOT active yet) ---
# Server-side CAPTCHA verification (a planned Phase C follow-up)
# will use a provider such as Cloudflare Turnstile. Only the
# PUBLIC site key may ever be added here, as VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY.
# The SECRET key belongs ONLY in the server function's secret
# store — never in this file, the repository, or the frontend.
